- *Machine-checked in Lean 4 / Z3 (algorithmic, bit-level encoding, and extreme-compression limit specifications):* arbitrary-$n$ matrix identities and pointwise Rayleigh distortion for Theorems 1–4; row-sum repair; arbitrary-finite-dimensional symmetric Galerkin V-cycle sandwich (`vcycle_upper_bound_of_galerkin_sandwich`, $B^top = B$); the full $A$-inner-product single-level operator step of Theorem 6 (`monotone_effectiveness_operator`, deriving the coarse-comparison inequality from $P, T, R, B_("amp")$ given `happrox`, without assuming `hE`); both directions of the $beta^2 < p$ frontier; rational budget/pruned-retention certificates (`norm_num`); arbitrary-depth induction on the *scalar* four-phase effectiveness recurrence `fourPhaseEff` (`four_phase_recurrence_induction`, `four_phase_arbitrary_depth_induction`, proving $e_0 >= 1/17$ and $e_0 >= 1/9$ for all depths $D in NN$); the $2 times 2$ counterexamples; all 16 public theorems (+ 3 internal helpers) in `BitLimits.lean` covering the line-loss identity, exact-prefix threshold (given $rho^2(sigma+D)=D$), arbitrary-$n$ determinant-ratio identity, 3-vertex grounded-SDDM sign-vs-ternary separation, arbitrary-$r$ ternary threshold-cut bound (given Kirchhoff flux `gap_k * cap_k <= sigma`), unit-path lower bound (for $sigma = 1/(r+1)$), local frozen-word Loewner and arbitrary-spectrum Kantorovich bounds (given variational/spectral-weight premises), projective packing separation, and harmonic-bin minimax error (cross-checked by 21 UNSAT + 2 SAT obligations in `proofs/z3/verify_bit_limits_z3.py`); and exhaustive bit-vector (`BitVec`) verification in `proofs/z3/verify_bit_encodings_z3.py` (12 UNSAT + 1 SAT) of nibble pack/unpack bijectivity over all 256 pairs, `standalone_amg.cu` row-aligned byte disjointness and in-bounds addressing, non-tautological piecewise encoder-to-decoder round-trips for both `bitfsai.cuh` offset-binary `INT4` and `standalone_amg.cu` two's-complement `INT4` (proving unused codes `0` and `8` are n